1
00:00:14,889 --> 00:00:17,308
<i>Why the hell are you doing this to me?</i>

2
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:18,226
<i>Why?</i>

3
00:00:18,309 --> 00:00:20,437
"Why?" That's a bit hurtful.

4
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:21,813
I just

5
00:00:22,313 --> 00:00:23,982
want to be you.

6
00:00:25,066 --> 00:00:26,026
<i>Do you understand?</i>

7
00:00:40,081 --> 00:00:41,249
You are just

8
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:43,043
jealous of me.

9
00:00:43,668 --> 00:00:47,005
You're dying of jealousy
because you want to be me.

10
00:00:47,088 --> 00:00:47,922
Aren't you?

11
00:00:50,508 --> 00:00:52,635
Shut up, you son of a bitch!

12
00:00:58,349 --> 00:00:59,225
This bastard

13
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:02,103
isn't dead.

14
00:01:04,272 --> 00:01:05,398
He's still alive.

15
00:01:43,186 --> 00:01:46,189
MOUSETRAP

16
00:01:46,272 --> 00:01:49,192
You won the Best New Writer award
for <i>Interview</i>.

17
00:01:49,275 --> 00:01:52,904
And you were even praised as a genius
after <i>Evil Always Prevails</i>.

18
00:01:52,987 --> 00:01:55,740
So what made you
suddenly go into seclusion?

19
00:01:56,366 --> 00:01:59,494
I think "seclusion"
might be a bit dramatic.

20
00:01:59,577 --> 00:02:00,745
How should I put this?

21
00:02:00,829 --> 00:02:02,872
A talentless writer

22
00:02:03,414 --> 00:02:06,668
was floundering on blank pages

23
00:02:08,002 --> 00:02:11,923
and eventually realized
the well had run dry.

24
00:02:12,006 --> 00:02:16,136
When I was a third year in high school,
my parents passed away at the same time,

25
00:02:16,219 --> 00:02:18,429
and I went through
panic disorder afterward.

26
00:02:18,513 --> 00:02:20,765
- It was fine for a while.
- I see.

27
00:02:20,849 --> 00:02:24,435
Then it started again.

28
00:02:24,936 --> 00:02:27,730
I think it hit me pretty hard
at that time.

29
00:02:28,606 --> 00:02:30,191
I see.

30
00:02:30,275 --> 00:02:33,486
So naturally, I guess
I started hiding from the world.

31
00:02:33,570 --> 00:02:36,239
Kind of like the rat in the book. Yeah.

32
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:45,415
What the hell are you talking about?
He's not dead? So that's fake?

33
00:02:45,498 --> 00:02:48,543
You said that's his job.
The guy who said Yu-min was dead.

34
00:02:48,626 --> 00:02:50,461
Yeah, identity fraud.

35
00:02:52,422 --> 00:02:54,716
Damn, those fucking bastards…

36
00:02:54,799 --> 00:02:57,468
- Let's go. We have someone to meet.
- Who now?

37
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:00,388
SAFER COMMUNITIES WITH DONGBU POLICE

38
00:03:03,224 --> 00:03:04,392
Man, it's hot.

39
00:03:05,643 --> 00:03:06,603
Hello.

40
00:03:07,478 --> 00:03:08,980
You're here.

41
00:03:09,063 --> 00:03:12,692
You didn't just show up with your novel
after all those years.

42
00:03:13,526 --> 00:03:15,361
You brought trouble too. Like your name.

43
00:03:15,445 --> 00:03:16,738
Right.

44
00:03:16,821 --> 00:03:18,573
I'm sorry for the trouble.

45
00:03:18,656 --> 00:03:20,950
Oh, it's okay.
We've gotta catch the impersonator.

46
00:03:22,577 --> 00:03:25,830
But why this police station?
It's not even close to your place.

47
00:03:26,414 --> 00:03:27,540
Just because.

48
00:03:27,624 --> 00:03:29,709
It's a bigger police station.

49
00:03:32,962 --> 00:03:33,838
Right.

50
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:37,800
Anyway, I'm sure our lawyer here
will take care of this.

51
00:03:38,301 --> 00:03:40,261
- All right, let's get in.
- Let's go.

52
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:45,725
It gets so hot so quickly.

53
00:03:47,518 --> 00:03:50,521
Can we also request personal protection?

54
00:03:50,605 --> 00:03:55,068
Did the impersonator threaten
or intimidate you?

55
00:03:55,652 --> 00:03:57,570
Not exactly.

56
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:02,742
But I heard he showed up at my reunion
saying he was Je Moon-jae.

57
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:04,535
And then,

58
00:04:04,619 --> 00:04:07,747
I heard one of my old classmates
died mysteriously.

59
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:09,540
And his kid was kidnapped too.

60
00:04:10,375 --> 00:04:12,377
- Oh, that case?
- Yes.

61
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:14,879
How could your old classmates
mistake him for you?

62
00:04:15,755 --> 00:04:17,674
I know, right? Well…

63
00:04:23,012 --> 00:04:25,223
They said he looked exactly

64
00:04:25,932 --> 00:04:27,267
like me.

65
00:04:28,476 --> 00:04:32,355
She was your editor-in-chief
when you got the Best New Writer award?

66
00:04:32,981 --> 00:04:35,942
Then why the hell is she publishing
a book with that rat bastard?

67
00:04:36,025 --> 00:04:39,320
How could she not tell the difference
between you and that rat bastard?

68
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:41,406
We barely ever met.

69
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:44,575
We mostly communicated by email,
so it's possible.

70
00:04:44,659 --> 00:04:47,620
It's because I'm a reclusive writer
who only uses a pen name.

71
00:04:47,704 --> 00:04:49,747
Did you fucking commit a crime or what?

72
00:04:49,831 --> 00:04:52,250
What are you, a thief?
Why hide your name? Damn it.

73
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:54,085
That's just how writers…

74
00:04:55,753 --> 00:04:57,839
That's just how a lot of people are.

75
00:04:57,922 --> 00:04:59,882
But that bastard didn't use the pen name.

76
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:02,051
He's using your actual name, Je Moon-jae.

77
00:05:02,135 --> 00:05:04,095
Like he's the real Je Moon-jae.

78
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:06,764
Come on.
Even his book's called <i>The Rat</i>. Fuck.

79
00:05:10,643 --> 00:05:11,477
Hey, by the way,

80
00:05:12,603 --> 00:05:14,564
how did the story end?

81
00:05:15,648 --> 00:05:17,984
You know the story. The old folklore.

82
00:05:18,067 --> 00:05:21,154
About a rat eating fingernails
and turning into a person.

83
00:05:21,237 --> 00:05:23,239
- Yeah.
- Yeah, you know…

84
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:24,532
How did it end?

85
00:05:25,366 --> 00:05:26,534
It was…

86
00:05:28,745 --> 00:05:29,746
a happy ending.

87
00:05:29,829 --> 00:05:30,830
Right? Damn it.

88
00:05:30,913 --> 00:05:32,832
Right? It's a happy ending, huh?

89
00:05:32,915 --> 00:05:35,752
Not some fucked-up ending
or anything, right?

90
00:05:35,835 --> 00:05:38,546
Yeah. Folklores are all about
good defeating evil.

91
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:47,055
But are you sure you're the good guy?

92
00:05:49,891 --> 00:05:53,186
You look exactly like some bastard I know.

93
00:05:55,313 --> 00:05:56,147
Oh.

94
00:05:56,689 --> 00:05:59,067
I think you're saying

95
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:01,194
I should prove that I'm Je Moon-jae.

96
00:06:03,237 --> 00:06:06,532
My publisher put out his book
when he won the Best New Writer award.

97
00:06:06,616 --> 00:06:07,825
I was the editor-in-chief.

98
00:06:08,451 --> 00:06:09,827
Right.

99
00:06:11,954 --> 00:06:14,791
Can two people really look that alike?
They're not even twins.

100
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:17,627
Maybe

101
00:06:18,127 --> 00:06:20,671
he wanted to look like me

102
00:06:21,172 --> 00:06:22,965
because he wanted to steal my life.

103
00:06:24,175 --> 00:06:25,093
Plastic surgery?

104
00:06:25,176 --> 00:06:29,555
Well, whether he got surgery or not,
he can't look exactly like me.

105
00:06:29,639 --> 00:06:32,934
I guess, if you look closely enough,
there have to be some differences.

106
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:39,107
I don't care who's who.

107
00:06:40,066 --> 00:06:43,277
I just need to know who the killer is.
The bad guy.

108
00:06:45,238 --> 00:06:46,406
The bad guy?

109
00:06:50,368 --> 00:06:51,244
I don't know.

110
00:06:51,327 --> 00:06:53,079
I don't think there's a bad guy.

111
00:06:53,579 --> 00:06:55,706
I think there's only the survivor.

112
00:06:56,707 --> 00:07:00,086
I'm just saying
that's the situation he's creating.

113
00:07:03,172 --> 00:07:04,465
Is there anything else?

114
00:07:04,549 --> 00:07:05,383
Oh, right.

115
00:07:17,395 --> 00:07:18,229
COMPLAINT

116
00:07:18,312 --> 00:07:20,189
COMPLAINANT: JE MOON-JAE
ACCUSED: JE MOON-JAE

117
00:07:23,568 --> 00:07:25,069
Hey, do you know me?

118
00:07:28,364 --> 00:07:31,492
Je Moon-jae. The name sounds familiar.

119
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:33,953
Have we met before?

120
00:07:34,036 --> 00:07:35,997
The name rings a bell.

121
00:07:37,748 --> 00:07:39,041
No.

122
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:41,878
- But why you?
- What?

123
00:07:41,961 --> 00:07:44,755
Why the hell is he so desperate
to take what's yours?

124
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:47,675
Do you two know each other?

125
00:07:49,093 --> 00:07:53,181
I don't know.
I was wondering the same thing. Why me?

126
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,602
Then what about me? Damn it.

127
00:07:57,685 --> 00:07:58,853
Why me?

128
00:08:00,104 --> 00:08:03,774
Why am I mixed up in your problem?

129
00:08:05,359 --> 00:08:07,487
There must be a police station
near your house.

130
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:11,949
Why did you come all the way here
to file a complaint?

131
00:08:16,287 --> 00:08:18,456
I went to my friend's funeral

132
00:08:18,539 --> 00:08:21,417
and heard you guys
were investigating his case.

133
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:25,713
I thought filing the complaint
at the same station might help.

134
00:08:25,796 --> 00:08:26,631
Doesn't that help?

135
00:08:33,137 --> 00:08:34,555
I'll get going now.

136
00:08:49,612 --> 00:08:50,488
Hey.

137
00:08:52,990 --> 00:08:54,492
This should be it.

138
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:56,410
Did it move?

139
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:59,205
NOVEL "THE RAT"

140
00:08:59,288 --> 00:09:01,332
Hey, it's Han Ji-hye, right?

141
00:09:01,832 --> 00:09:04,126
- The editor-in-chief of your first novel.
- Yeah.

142
00:09:04,627 --> 00:09:07,296
She started her own publishing house.
Damn it.

143
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:09,173
You should've checked before coming.

144
00:09:10,258 --> 00:09:11,717
Damn.

145
00:09:11,801 --> 00:09:12,802
What now?

146
00:09:12,885 --> 00:09:14,720
We go to this address, obviously.

147
00:09:15,304 --> 00:09:17,932
We also have to tell her
that bastard is deceiving her.

148
00:09:18,516 --> 00:09:20,184
Hey, who knows?

149
00:09:20,685 --> 00:09:22,270
Maybe she'll be our cat.

150
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:26,566
You know, in that story,

151
00:09:26,649 --> 00:09:29,652
the cat catches the rat that turned human.

152
00:09:29,735 --> 00:09:33,823
The cat will probably know
who the fake one is.

153
00:09:35,157 --> 00:09:36,367
Let's go. Fuck.

154
00:09:36,867 --> 00:09:37,702
THE RAT

155
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:56,846
What's wrong?

156
00:09:58,139 --> 00:09:59,307
Nothing, just…

157
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:01,267
It feels unfamiliar.

158
00:10:01,767 --> 00:10:04,395
- What do you mean?
- You weren't like this before.

159
00:10:04,478 --> 00:10:08,441
You hated meeting people.
You hated coming to the publisher too.

160
00:10:09,984 --> 00:10:12,987
I only asked you to stay for coffee
out of courtesy.

161
00:10:13,070 --> 00:10:16,032
Yet here you are, having a cup of coffee.
I find it unfamiliar.

162
00:10:18,701 --> 00:10:20,369
Was I that bad?

163
00:10:20,453 --> 00:10:22,830
I guess your panic disorder
is all better now.

164
00:10:23,372 --> 00:10:24,248
That's good.

165
00:10:27,251 --> 00:10:28,210
Just a moment.

166
00:10:29,795 --> 00:10:30,630
Hello?

167
00:10:32,131 --> 00:10:33,924
<i>Is this Ms. Han, the editor-in-chief?</i>

168
00:10:34,967 --> 00:10:38,179
You probably don't remember me.
This is Je Moon-jae.

169
00:10:41,057 --> 00:10:44,226
<i>You helped me a lot</i>
<i>when I won the Best New Writer award.</i>

170
00:10:46,270 --> 00:10:48,397
I have something to tell you in person.

171
00:10:49,065 --> 00:10:51,108
I saw the video of the book launch event.

172
00:10:51,192 --> 00:10:52,401
That wasn't me.

173
00:10:52,485 --> 00:10:54,570
<i>That guy's deceiving you.</i>

174
00:10:54,654 --> 00:10:56,489
Hey, um…

175
00:10:57,156 --> 00:10:58,783
He took everything from me

176
00:10:58,866 --> 00:11:01,118
while I was stuck at home
with a panic disorder.

177
00:11:01,202 --> 00:11:03,079
It's a bit complicated to explain.

178
00:11:03,162 --> 00:11:05,039
I'm near the publisher right now.

179
00:11:05,122 --> 00:11:07,124
I'll explain everything in person.

180
00:11:07,208 --> 00:11:08,834
Could you spare me a few minutes?

181
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:30,481
You're the only person
who can help me right now.

182
00:11:31,482 --> 00:11:33,734
Can you prove
you're really Mr. Je Moon-jae?

183
00:11:34,318 --> 00:11:36,237
You'll have to do it for me.

184
00:11:43,619 --> 00:11:45,955
<i>The Rat</i>. Did you write it yourself?

185
00:11:46,747 --> 00:11:48,541
No, I didn't write that.

186
00:11:48,624 --> 00:11:50,501
I think that guy wrote it.

187
00:11:50,584 --> 00:11:52,545
He used my childhood,

188
00:11:52,628 --> 00:11:55,131
the story of my parents' death,
and things like that.

189
00:11:55,214 --> 00:11:58,968
I think he used my whole life
as a motif in the story.

190
00:11:59,051 --> 00:12:00,803
It's a long story.

191
00:12:00,886 --> 00:12:04,557
- I think he knew me from before.
- Wait. Hold on.

192
00:12:07,226 --> 00:12:09,645
The person who wrote <i>The Rat</i>
is Je Moon-jae.

193
00:12:09,729 --> 00:12:11,021
I'm sure of that.

194
00:12:11,105 --> 00:12:13,899
People can lie, but the writings can't.

195
00:12:13,983 --> 00:12:15,985
I've read his books
since his very first one.

196
00:12:16,068 --> 00:12:18,988
You think the guy
who copied and stole my entire life

197
00:12:19,071 --> 00:12:20,906
couldn't imitate my writing?

198
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:23,826
What happened to your panic disorder?
Are you all better now?

199
00:12:23,909 --> 00:12:24,952
No, I'm not.

200
00:12:25,035 --> 00:12:27,830
With all this happening,
I had no choice but to come out.

201
00:12:27,913 --> 00:12:31,375
Je Moon-jae wouldn't even be sitting here.
Unless he's all better now.

202
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:33,919
His panic disorder was really severe.

203
00:12:34,003 --> 00:12:36,172
That's what I'm saying here.

204
00:12:36,255 --> 00:12:38,048
I may look fine on the outside,

205
00:12:38,632 --> 00:12:40,593
but I'm barely getting by on meds.

206
00:12:40,676 --> 00:12:42,261
This is for my panic disorder--

207
00:12:42,344 --> 00:12:44,597
- Get up. We have to go!
- Huh? Why?

208
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:47,141
- Come on. Hurry.
- Why?

209
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:59,278
- Did you get all the CCTV footage?
- No, I couldn't.

210
00:13:00,529 --> 00:13:02,531
Do you remember the suspect's appearance?

211
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:03,991
Oh, there.

212
00:13:04,533 --> 00:13:05,367
Yeah.

213
00:13:07,161 --> 00:13:10,581
If something like this happened,
you should've called me.

214
00:13:10,664 --> 00:13:12,291
But instead, you called 112.

215
00:13:13,083 --> 00:13:14,960
This is driving me crazy. Seriously.

216
00:13:15,044 --> 00:13:18,506
Did you think he'd just show you his ID
if you asked for it?

217
00:13:19,089 --> 00:13:21,091
I wanted to check myself first.

218
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:24,887
I wasn't sure since he said
his panic disorder kept him stuck at home.

219
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:27,723
Je Moon-jae
did have severe panic disorder.

220
00:13:29,642 --> 00:13:30,935
What's your conclusion?

221
00:13:31,435 --> 00:13:32,853
Huh? This is the fake one?

222
00:13:33,896 --> 00:13:36,357
He was with the thug
from the picture you showed me.

223
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:39,527
It would've been great
if you'd just let me catch him, you know?

224
00:13:40,027 --> 00:13:42,738
We're both busy people.
No need to waste our time like this.

225
00:13:42,822 --> 00:13:44,365
I fully understand.

226
00:13:44,448 --> 00:13:47,368
I'll call you if he contacts me again.

227
00:13:47,451 --> 00:13:49,787
Just catch that scammer who ran off.

228
00:13:51,205 --> 00:13:52,122
Look.

229
00:13:56,418 --> 00:13:58,254
He's not a scammer.

230
00:13:58,796 --> 00:14:00,005
He's a murderer.

231
00:14:01,549 --> 00:14:03,342
Yes, whatever he is.

232
00:14:11,225 --> 00:14:14,019
He was stuck at home
because of his panic disorder?

233
00:14:14,770 --> 00:14:16,939
KIDNAPPING CASE
FATHER FOUND DEAD IN THE HANGANG RIVER

234
00:14:17,022 --> 00:14:18,315
SUSPECT LINKED TO SHOOTING CASE

235
00:14:22,778 --> 00:14:24,655
Not one bastard is helping.

236
00:14:25,281 --> 00:14:27,867
Everywhere I look,
there are just damn enemies!

237
00:14:28,951 --> 00:14:30,160
You bastard!

238
00:14:30,244 --> 00:14:33,038
What the hell have you been doing
to cause this mess?

239
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:34,081
I don't know!

240
00:14:34,164 --> 00:14:37,334
How the hell can I tell you anything
when I don't know what's going on?

241
00:14:37,835 --> 00:14:39,837
No one is telling me a damn thing!

242
00:14:40,838 --> 00:14:42,506
How can I prove I'm really me?

243
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:45,509
Can you prove you're you?
How would you do that?

244
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:48,762
You fucking bastard!

245
00:14:49,263 --> 00:14:53,559
You need others to prove it, punk!
They know me better than I do.

246
00:14:53,642 --> 00:14:55,769
But why doesn't that work for you, punk?

247
00:14:55,853 --> 00:14:57,605
Why can't anyone prove it for you?!

248
00:14:57,688 --> 00:14:58,731
You bastard!

249
00:15:03,527 --> 00:15:04,987
Fuck!

250
00:15:11,952 --> 00:15:13,579
Forget proving it.

251
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:16,415
We have to lay low first.

252
00:15:25,841 --> 00:15:27,968
<i>What do you want me to do with him?</i>

253
00:15:28,469 --> 00:15:30,220
Look into him.

254
00:15:30,304 --> 00:15:32,514
Dig up everything about him.

255
00:15:34,391 --> 00:15:38,812
Turn over every rock to find out
if that bastard really is Je Moon-jae.

256
00:15:40,439 --> 00:15:41,523
Yeah.

257
00:15:41,607 --> 00:15:43,567
He never caused trouble
while he lived here.

258
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:45,861
He was always the first to say hello.

259
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:48,906
Like I said before, he did live here.

260
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:52,493
He's the guy who lives in this building.

261
00:15:52,576 --> 00:15:54,662
He got takeout
three or four times a month.

262
00:15:54,745 --> 00:15:56,372
<i>It's the Heineken guy.</i>

263
00:15:56,455 --> 00:16:00,042
<i>Once a week, every Friday,</i>
<i>four cans of Heineken.</i>

264
00:16:03,629 --> 00:16:07,383
Doesn't sound like someone
who stayed holed up with panic disorder.

265
00:16:31,031 --> 00:16:32,700
<i>We received a tip.</i>

266
00:16:45,254 --> 00:16:48,424
Can two people really look that alike?
They're not even twins.

267
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:49,341
Maybe

268
00:16:49,842 --> 00:16:52,636
he wanted to look like me

269
00:16:53,887 --> 00:16:56,056
<i>because he wanted to steal my life.</i>

270
00:16:57,099 --> 00:16:58,809
Which one is it?

271
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:10,821
So you're asking where I was
the first week of this month?

272
00:17:12,239 --> 00:17:15,868
That might be difficult for me to prove.

273
00:17:15,951 --> 00:17:18,370
Nobody remembers when it hurts them.

274
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:19,830
Is this one of those cases?

275
00:17:19,913 --> 00:17:21,290
No, it's not that.

276
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:25,419
That was right before my book came out,
so I was alone.

277
00:17:25,502 --> 00:17:27,337
There's no one who can vouch for me.

278
00:17:28,797 --> 00:17:30,007
Where were you?

279
00:17:30,090 --> 00:17:31,133
<i>At a vacation home.</i>

280
00:17:31,216 --> 00:17:34,762
It was right before my book came out,
so I wanted to focus on my writing.

281
00:17:35,345 --> 00:17:37,264
But why are you suspecting me?

282
00:17:37,347 --> 00:17:38,432
I'm the victim.

283
00:17:39,683 --> 00:17:42,936
Comes with the job.
That's how I make a living.

284
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:45,189
Either way, one of you is a fake.

285
00:17:45,272 --> 00:17:48,650
Just give me your alibi already
so you can walk free.

286
00:17:48,734 --> 00:17:52,029
Then I'll send you a link.
It has the rental's address.

287
00:17:52,112 --> 00:17:53,614
<i>You can check it out.</i>

288
00:17:54,114 --> 00:17:54,948
Well…

289
00:17:55,616 --> 00:17:56,575
Hello?

290
00:17:57,576 --> 00:17:58,577
Hello?

291
00:18:00,329 --> 00:18:02,581
This bastard, seriously. Damn it.

292
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:14,426
SKY SOUND VACATION HOME

293
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:17,638
<i>He's the man in the photo you sent.</i>

294
00:18:17,721 --> 00:18:19,765
<i>About ten days?</i>

295
00:18:19,848 --> 00:18:23,268
<i>Yes, he stayed for about ten days.</i>

296
00:18:28,232 --> 00:18:31,110
<i>He was on his laptop whenever I saw him.</i>

297
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:35,322
<i>His car was parked in the lot</i>
<i>for the entire ten days.</i>

298
00:18:35,405 --> 00:18:38,242
<i>There's so much to do around here,</i>
<i>but he never went out.</i>

299
00:18:39,201 --> 00:18:40,953
<i>I think he was a writer.</i>

300
00:18:41,036 --> 00:18:46,041
<i>I checked the CCTV footage just in case,</i>
<i>and it really was him.</i>

301
00:18:50,504 --> 00:18:52,089
Then was it you?

302
00:19:19,867 --> 00:19:23,245
Let's go. If the locals see us,
they'll get suspicious.

303
00:19:23,954 --> 00:19:25,789
- Did you sleep?
- Sort of.

304
00:19:26,582 --> 00:19:29,459
I must be getting old.
Fuck. I can't sleep in the car anymore.

305
00:19:43,807 --> 00:19:46,018
Maybe I should see
the editor-in-chief again.

306
00:19:46,518 --> 00:19:49,688
I couldn't tell her everything last time.
Should I call her?

307
00:19:54,151 --> 00:19:56,403
You look at me like my father did.

308
00:19:56,486 --> 00:19:58,280
How did he look at you?

309
00:19:58,363 --> 00:19:59,823
Like I was pathetic.

310
00:19:59,907 --> 00:20:01,366
What pathetic thing did you do?

311
00:20:02,534 --> 00:20:04,119
I don't know. He never told me.

312
00:20:04,912 --> 00:20:08,290
He looked at me like he knew everything
and I knew nothing.

313
00:20:08,790 --> 00:20:11,001
He'd been that way since I was a kid.

314
00:20:11,084 --> 00:20:13,712
Like he knew everything about the world.

315
00:20:13,795 --> 00:20:15,881
I bet he didn't even know
he'd die like that.

316
00:20:18,008 --> 00:20:19,635
That's how I'm looking at you.

317
00:20:22,346 --> 00:20:24,848
If we go see the editor-in-chief again,
we'll get caught.

318
00:20:25,349 --> 00:20:26,934
It's a pathetic and stupid thing to do.

319
00:20:28,185 --> 00:20:30,520
I don't get it.
How could she believe that bastard?

320
00:20:31,188 --> 00:20:32,022
Hey.

321
00:20:32,522 --> 00:20:35,567
He wrote a novel himself.
Maybe he's a better writer than you.

322
00:20:36,151 --> 00:20:37,945
Think of something while we lay low.

323
00:20:38,028 --> 00:20:39,738
Something only you have.

324
00:20:39,821 --> 00:20:43,158
Something he doesn't know and can't get.
Your very own alibi.

325
00:20:43,784 --> 00:20:44,826
Prove it with that.

326
00:20:51,750 --> 00:20:53,752
You said I'd get promoted, punk.

327
00:20:55,295 --> 00:20:58,632
- So you agreed to hand it to Major Crimes?
- What choice do I have?

328
00:20:59,132 --> 00:21:01,468
A tip, murder, and identity fraud.
The full package.

329
00:21:01,551 --> 00:21:05,097
We busted our asses for this,
and now Major Crimes gets all the credit.

330
00:21:05,597 --> 00:21:08,392
But sir, this is great.

331
00:21:08,892 --> 00:21:12,688
It's better not to get involved
with headache cases. Yes.

332
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:15,691
- Am I wrong?
- You're right.

333
00:21:16,358 --> 00:21:18,277
So you should drop it too.

334
00:21:18,777 --> 00:21:20,237
Drop the case, got it?

335
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:23,115
I got it. I'll stop.
I already handed over the files.

336
00:21:24,032 --> 00:21:24,950
Really?

337
00:21:25,742 --> 00:21:27,077
Yes, really.

338
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:28,453
You really need to stop.

339
00:21:29,579 --> 00:21:32,374
Have you been lied to your whole life?
I said I got it.

340
00:21:33,875 --> 00:21:35,460
You're not gonna stop, punk!

341
00:22:01,278 --> 00:22:04,364
Oh man. It's only been a few days,
and you already look…

342
00:22:05,073 --> 00:22:08,618
You might rot away
after a few years inside.

343
00:22:10,662 --> 00:22:12,998
Your real boss, Park Seung-gyu.

344
00:22:13,081 --> 00:22:16,376
He bolted overseas by himself
before the travel ban kicked in.

345
00:22:17,461 --> 00:22:18,712
It was quick. So quick.

346
00:22:18,795 --> 00:22:20,339
It was insanely quick.

347
00:22:21,256 --> 00:22:24,134
Major Crimes is taking over the case.
What are you gonna do?

348
00:22:24,217 --> 00:22:26,094
You're the only one who's screwed.

349
00:22:27,804 --> 00:22:30,766
Well, that thing
you were hiding in your shop.

350
00:22:30,849 --> 00:22:33,852
That cash box. What happened to it?

351
00:22:33,935 --> 00:22:35,395
It was empty.

352
00:22:36,146 --> 00:22:40,692
You thought you could do a few years
and live off your hidden cash?

353
00:22:41,443 --> 00:22:42,861
Understandable, yeah.

354
00:22:43,904 --> 00:22:45,739
I would've thought so too.

355
00:22:45,822 --> 00:22:47,532
Wait. Why am I here?

356
00:22:47,616 --> 00:22:48,492
Right.

357
00:22:49,242 --> 00:22:51,244
I've got something to ask you.

358
00:22:51,328 --> 00:22:52,829
Kwak Sang-cheol.

359
00:22:54,956 --> 00:22:56,041
Do you know him?

360
00:22:56,541 --> 00:23:01,463
I looked into the gang that Noja was in,
and I found this guy there.

361
00:23:01,546 --> 00:23:05,717
He killed someone
and ran off to the Philippines.

362
00:23:05,801 --> 00:23:08,762
Look here.
This one's a real vicious bastard.

363
00:23:09,554 --> 00:23:10,472
Do you know him?

364
00:23:12,224 --> 00:23:13,600
MURDER
KWAK SANG-CHEOL (43)

365
00:23:13,683 --> 00:23:15,769
Wait. What's this?

366
00:23:17,896 --> 00:23:20,440
Why does this bastard look like you?

367
00:23:20,941 --> 00:23:22,025
What the hell?

368
00:23:22,109 --> 00:23:23,360
Why do you two look alike?

369
00:23:24,361 --> 00:23:26,905
Huh? You really do look like him.

370
00:23:27,948 --> 00:23:29,032
I get it now.

371
00:23:30,784 --> 00:23:32,244
That's right. Park Seung-gyu.

372
00:23:32,828 --> 00:23:34,955
He runs an identity fraud ring.

373
00:23:35,038 --> 00:23:37,082
So this means

374
00:23:38,041 --> 00:23:39,459
that bastard

375
00:23:40,085 --> 00:23:43,880
might have turned this bastard
into this bastard.

376
00:23:54,182 --> 00:23:55,475
You fucking bastard.

377
00:23:56,059 --> 00:23:58,687
If the prosecution finds out
you're Kwak Sang-cheol,

378
00:23:59,271 --> 00:24:02,107
you won't be celebrating
your 70th birthday outside.

379
00:24:05,735 --> 00:24:07,821
Sang-cheol, you know what?

380
00:24:09,698 --> 00:24:11,741
I'm the only one who knows about this.

381
00:24:16,997 --> 00:24:21,209
Fuck. The pigs even cleaned this out.

382
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:23,295
We busted our asses just to pay taxes.

383
00:24:23,378 --> 00:24:26,089
Sir, I already sent someone abroad
using your ID.

384
00:24:26,173 --> 00:24:27,674
You should get changed now.

385
00:24:27,757 --> 00:24:29,217
But this…

386
00:24:29,801 --> 00:24:31,720
The pigs didn't take this.

387
00:24:32,471 --> 00:24:36,558
The pigs love showing off.
They'd have leaked this already.

388
00:24:37,809 --> 00:24:42,314
Those bastards are just civil servants
who'd do anything for a promotion.

389
00:24:52,657 --> 00:24:53,700
So…

390
00:24:56,244 --> 00:24:58,205
Myeong-su's the one who took it.

391
00:24:59,998 --> 00:25:03,376
He was probably the fucking one
who sent the tip too.

392
00:25:03,877 --> 00:25:08,548
That bastard has multiple names
and identities.

393
00:25:08,632 --> 00:25:11,593
Fake identities that pay taxes
and get regular checkups.

394
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:16,515
Seung-gyu used to find places
for the wanted higher-ups to hide

395
00:25:17,015 --> 00:25:19,351
and make fake identities for them.

396
00:25:19,851 --> 00:25:23,313
And then
he turned identity fraud into a business.

397
00:25:23,396 --> 00:25:25,315
He caught the higher-ups' attention.

398
00:25:25,398 --> 00:25:28,276
And he branched out
into online gambling and loan sharking.

399
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:30,320
That puny runt's come a long way.

400
00:25:31,738 --> 00:25:35,200
The guy who left the country?
No way that was really Seung-gyu.

401
00:25:35,700 --> 00:25:38,745
He would never leave the country
without fixing this problem.

402
00:25:38,828 --> 00:25:39,663
What problem?

403
00:25:39,746 --> 00:25:41,540
The tip.

404
00:25:41,623 --> 00:25:43,416
But your names aren't on the tip.

405
00:25:43,500 --> 00:25:45,627
We're all tangled up in this.

406
00:25:45,710 --> 00:25:48,838
If you dig into our pasts,
we're all connected somehow.

407
00:25:48,922 --> 00:25:51,258
Seung-gyu has to kill
everyone connected to the tip.

408
00:25:51,341 --> 00:25:52,801
Why?

409
00:25:52,884 --> 00:25:55,929
If Noja or I open our mouths,
he's screwed.

410
00:25:56,513 --> 00:26:00,267
He threw away countless empty shells
after taking what was inside.

411
00:26:00,350 --> 00:26:01,560
Is that why you sent it?

412
00:26:01,643 --> 00:26:04,563
So you could screw everyone over
and be the sole survivor?

413
00:26:05,939 --> 00:26:09,734
It had to be someone
who knew more about this than I did.

414
00:26:11,111 --> 00:26:12,404
And who's that?

415
00:26:15,448 --> 00:26:16,783
Do you have a cigarette?

416
00:26:17,867 --> 00:26:19,202
Yeah, I've got one.

417
00:26:31,923 --> 00:26:35,552
We were all doing fine before this, right?

418
00:26:36,761 --> 00:26:40,181
This is all because of that bastard.
He must've sent the tip too.

419
00:26:40,265 --> 00:26:41,433
That bastard?

420
00:26:42,017 --> 00:26:42,851
Who?

421
00:26:45,770 --> 00:26:47,814
The guy who should've died
and disappeared.

422
00:26:48,315 --> 00:26:50,942
Everything went to shit
because he came back from the dead.

423
00:27:31,441 --> 00:27:32,275
Yeah.

424
00:27:34,069 --> 00:27:35,028
So?

425
00:27:35,737 --> 00:27:36,780
What?

426
00:27:37,405 --> 00:27:40,992
Goddamn it. Bring me something solid.

427
00:27:41,493 --> 00:27:42,494
Something irrefutable.

428
00:27:46,539 --> 00:27:47,707
Who was it?

429
00:27:49,626 --> 00:27:50,960
None of your business.

430
00:27:52,837 --> 00:27:55,048
Where are we? Where are we going?

431
00:27:55,131 --> 00:27:57,634
A good place to lay low.

432
00:27:58,468 --> 00:28:00,011
Near my hometown.

433
00:28:02,263 --> 00:28:06,643
Isn't it risky going back to your hometown
with the cops after us?

434
00:28:08,103 --> 00:28:10,772
Maybe it's because my life
is about to be over,

435
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:13,441
but I miss my hometown.

436
00:28:16,027 --> 00:28:17,153
Who's there?

437
00:28:20,115 --> 00:28:21,157
The proof

438
00:28:21,825 --> 00:28:23,660
that I'm really me.

439
00:28:26,037 --> 00:28:27,539
Hey, when we get there,

440
00:28:27,622 --> 00:28:31,793
hide for a few days
and think about who you really are.

441
00:28:32,961 --> 00:28:35,505
Just sit alone in the middle of the night

442
00:28:36,005 --> 00:28:39,259
and think about
what kind of bastard you are.

443
00:28:39,342 --> 00:28:42,679
And think about how there's no one
who can prove who you really are.

444
00:28:43,763 --> 00:28:46,307
You no-good bastard.

445
00:28:47,892 --> 00:28:48,935
Damn it.

446
00:29:05,618 --> 00:29:09,372
The cars sound like
the waves in the ocean.

447
00:29:10,373 --> 00:29:12,792
The sound of waves
in the middle of the city.

448
00:29:12,876 --> 00:29:16,004
I envy your senses.

449
00:29:21,885 --> 00:29:25,263
By the way, when are you finishing
the second volume?

450
00:29:25,346 --> 00:29:28,224
It should come out
while the first volume's still hot.

451
00:29:28,725 --> 00:29:30,226
How come

452
00:29:30,310 --> 00:29:32,604
you showed up so suddenly
without telling me?

453
00:29:34,314 --> 00:29:35,148
Oh.

454
00:29:35,648 --> 00:29:38,902
I was just passing by.
I was curious about the second volume too.

455
00:29:39,402 --> 00:29:40,278
Come on.

456
00:29:40,361 --> 00:29:42,489
You left in a hurry
after that call yesterday.

457
00:29:42,572 --> 00:29:44,032
So I thought you were busy,

458
00:29:44,115 --> 00:29:45,742
but I guess not.

459
00:29:46,659 --> 00:29:49,329
Come on, tell me. Why did you really come?

460
00:29:49,412 --> 00:29:51,122
Not about the second volume, right?

461
00:29:52,540 --> 00:29:54,793
No, I really came to ask about it.

462
00:29:54,876 --> 00:29:57,962
It's good. When will you finish it?

463
00:29:59,380 --> 00:30:00,298
Come on.

464
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:03,176
My writing…

465
00:30:08,723 --> 00:30:10,683
Still doubting me after reading it?

466
00:30:16,022 --> 00:30:17,106
I mean…

467
00:30:18,024 --> 00:30:20,318
Things don't always go as planned, huh?

468
00:30:23,196 --> 00:30:26,032
I guess I dropped by too suddenly, right?

469
00:30:26,115 --> 00:30:27,575
Just hold on.

470
00:30:28,076 --> 00:30:29,160
Right now, I'm…

471
00:30:29,661 --> 00:30:30,995
Well,

472
00:30:31,746 --> 00:30:33,456
I'm at a crossroads.

473
00:30:33,540 --> 00:30:38,211
And I'm not entirely sure what to choose.
Could you give me some time?

474
00:30:53,226 --> 00:30:54,936
<i>The guy who should've died</i>
<i>and disappeared.</i>

475
00:30:55,019 --> 00:30:57,522
<i>Everything went to shit</i>
<i>because he came back from the dead.</i>

476
00:31:10,034 --> 00:31:11,369
Let's help each other out.

477
00:31:12,620 --> 00:31:15,039
You don't want to live
as the front either.

478
00:31:17,333 --> 00:31:19,419
I've got a plan.

479
00:31:21,838 --> 00:31:22,839
Do you wanna hear it?

480
00:31:25,383 --> 00:31:28,928
<i>That bastard learned some bad shit</i>
<i>while he was held by Seung-gyu.</i>

481
00:31:29,637 --> 00:31:33,099
<i>He killed a homeless guy</i>
<i>and committed identity fraud.</i>

482
00:31:33,182 --> 00:31:34,142
How?

483
00:31:34,225 --> 00:31:35,935
How did you help him?

484
00:31:36,019 --> 00:31:37,896
I made him a dead man.

485
00:31:38,396 --> 00:31:41,065
I've got a guy I know
at a public hospital morgue.

486
00:31:41,149 --> 00:31:42,817
He was in some gambling debt.

487
00:31:44,319 --> 00:31:47,322
We cremated the homeless guy
under this punk's name.

488
00:31:47,405 --> 00:31:49,741
And he disappeared for a while.

489
00:31:50,491 --> 00:31:52,702
Then he showed up the other day.

490
00:31:53,411 --> 00:31:54,913
And his face had changed.

491
00:31:55,413 --> 00:31:56,915
This bastard

492
00:31:57,498 --> 00:31:58,833
became this bastard.

493
00:31:59,375 --> 00:32:00,793
And he called himself the Rat.

494
00:32:00,877 --> 00:32:03,254
He started talking complete horse crap

495
00:32:03,338 --> 00:32:06,925
about petty jealousy creating a monster.

496
00:32:10,511 --> 00:32:11,596
What bullshit is that?

497
00:32:11,679 --> 00:32:13,932
Exactly. Why the hell should I care?

498
00:32:14,015 --> 00:32:17,685
I just wanted to quit being the front
and live a decent life.

499
00:32:17,769 --> 00:32:21,064
He came to me saying
I'd better get in shape for prison.

500
00:32:21,981 --> 00:32:23,900
He said I'd be rich after a year or two.

501
00:32:24,734 --> 00:32:26,486
Can you tell them apart?

502
00:32:27,320 --> 00:32:28,655
Well, that depends on

503
00:32:29,322 --> 00:32:32,659
whether we can make a deal, doesn't it?

504
00:32:33,159 --> 00:32:34,786
NAME: SEO YU-MIN

505
00:33:01,354 --> 00:33:03,022
The Rat…

506
00:34:08,337 --> 00:34:11,424
Noja, you know the picture you sent me?

507
00:34:11,924 --> 00:34:14,427
The girl. The one with the tattoo.

508
00:34:15,094 --> 00:34:16,304
She died.

509
00:34:16,387 --> 00:34:18,890
I checked the CCTV footage.

510
00:34:19,474 --> 00:34:21,517
And the suspect is…

511
00:34:22,393 --> 00:34:23,644
It's him.

512
00:34:24,854 --> 00:34:26,898
His father was a writer too.

513
00:34:26,981 --> 00:34:29,067
So I started digging into his father,

514
00:34:29,150 --> 00:34:31,861
<i>and I found some shocking evidence.</i>

515
00:34:52,298 --> 00:34:55,468
Why did you take so long
to go to a convenience store?

516
00:35:06,437 --> 00:35:09,482
Are we even allowed to be here?
We didn't get permission.

517
00:35:11,567 --> 00:35:12,610
This is

518
00:35:13,945 --> 00:35:16,447
where a married monk I know used to live.

519
00:35:17,698 --> 00:35:20,618
He opened a small prayer hall in town
and stopped coming here.

520
00:35:21,536 --> 00:35:23,204
Can you even sleep here?

521
00:35:25,581 --> 00:35:28,042
I guess your life's not tiring enough.

522
00:35:31,587 --> 00:35:33,840
I don't know. I'm hungry.

523
00:35:40,847 --> 00:35:42,348
Let me ask you something.

524
00:35:43,349 --> 00:35:44,225
What?

525
00:35:47,061 --> 00:35:48,896
Where were you early this month?

526
00:35:50,690 --> 00:35:53,317
What do you mean? I was home.

527
00:35:57,864 --> 00:36:00,783
I told you.
I didn't leave my house for three years.

528
00:36:01,617 --> 00:36:02,743
Why?

529
00:36:03,327 --> 00:36:06,831
Is there anyone who can prove
that you never left home?

530
00:36:07,957 --> 00:36:09,167
There used to be.

531
00:36:10,001 --> 00:36:11,878
But he died. Soo-hyun.

532
00:36:12,587 --> 00:36:13,796
Oh, right.

533
00:36:14,881 --> 00:36:16,340
So there's no one now?

534
00:36:22,722 --> 00:36:24,140
Why?

535
00:36:25,183 --> 00:36:27,310
The girl who was with you and the Rat.

536
00:36:28,269 --> 00:36:30,563
- The one with the ankle tattoo.
- Yeah.

537
00:36:31,147 --> 00:36:31,981
She died.

538
00:36:36,652 --> 00:36:38,196
But how did she die?

539
00:36:39,655 --> 00:36:41,073
You killed her.

540
00:36:43,242 --> 00:36:44,076
Huh?

541
00:36:44,160 --> 00:36:46,954
The police got the CCTV footage
from the crime scene.

542
00:36:47,038 --> 00:36:48,372
And you were there.

543
00:36:51,918 --> 00:36:52,752
Then

544
00:36:53,711 --> 00:36:55,504
it must've been that bastard.

545
00:36:55,588 --> 00:36:57,423
I never left home. How could I kill her?

546
00:36:57,506 --> 00:36:59,383
The police files say

547
00:36:59,467 --> 00:37:01,052
tons of people saw you

548
00:37:01,135 --> 00:37:04,639
around the apartment
you were supposedly hiding in, bastard.

549
00:37:04,722 --> 00:37:08,059
How did a bastard who never left home
buy beer every week?

550
00:37:08,142 --> 00:37:10,394
Then that must also be that bastard…

551
00:37:12,146 --> 00:37:14,023
Noja, do you suspect me?

552
00:37:14,106 --> 00:37:15,149
Yeah.

553
00:37:27,870 --> 00:37:29,038
JE GEUN-U
CRITICS AWARD WINNER

554
00:37:30,039 --> 00:37:31,666
They're your parents, right?

555
00:37:31,749 --> 00:37:33,793
Je Geun-u. Han Yeong-hui.

556
00:37:34,627 --> 00:37:37,088
Wow, the whole family
turned up for his award.

557
00:37:37,588 --> 00:37:38,798
But…

558
00:37:38,881 --> 00:37:39,882
What's this?

559
00:37:40,633 --> 00:37:42,009
Is that you?

560
00:37:43,970 --> 00:37:45,221
That's not you, is it?

561
00:37:47,515 --> 00:37:48,391
Hey.

562
00:37:50,142 --> 00:37:51,852
Who are you? You fucking asshole.

563
00:37:53,938 --> 00:37:57,275
After I entered the Buddhist path,

564
00:37:57,775 --> 00:38:02,947
I was taught that attachment
is the root of suffering.

565
00:38:03,739 --> 00:38:07,827
What future are you so desperate to know
that you came all this way?

566
00:38:08,619 --> 00:38:09,620
Noja.

567
00:38:11,414 --> 00:38:12,915
Where's Noja right now?

568
00:38:13,624 --> 00:38:15,793
Who is Noja?

569
00:38:22,717 --> 00:38:24,135
Your junior from high school.

570
00:38:24,927 --> 00:38:26,595
The guy who set this up for you.

571
00:38:28,806 --> 00:38:30,891
I think

572
00:38:31,475 --> 00:38:35,688
you might have come here by mistake.

573
00:38:41,819 --> 00:38:43,863
Isn't this photoshopped?

574
00:38:43,946 --> 00:38:45,656
It's a screenshot, punk.

575
00:38:46,157 --> 00:38:48,909
That picture was in a magazine
called <i>Literary Review</i>.

576
00:38:48,993 --> 00:38:51,037
They're your parents, right?

577
00:38:51,120 --> 00:38:52,121
They are, but…

578
00:38:52,204 --> 00:38:56,083
That was issued
a year before you were born.

579
00:38:56,167 --> 00:38:59,545
But, fuck, that's Je Moon-jae there,
all grown up.

580
00:39:00,546 --> 00:39:01,380
No.

581
00:39:01,464 --> 00:39:05,968
My parents said they had me late
because they struggled to have a kid.

582
00:39:07,053 --> 00:39:08,179
Who is this kid?

583
00:39:08,971 --> 00:39:10,806
It says Je Moon-jae. You bastard!

584
00:39:13,893 --> 00:39:15,436
I'll ask you again.

585
00:39:17,188 --> 00:39:18,856
Just answer my question.

586
00:39:19,648 --> 00:39:21,150
Who are you, you bastard?

587
00:39:27,073 --> 00:39:31,243
MANBULAM

588
00:39:39,668 --> 00:39:41,128
FOUND HIM

589
00:39:49,804 --> 00:39:53,641
Why the fuck are you giving me
this shit too?

590
00:39:53,724 --> 00:39:55,976
You can't explain anything right now,
you bastard!

591
00:39:56,060 --> 00:39:57,144
Explain how?

592
00:39:58,270 --> 00:40:00,689
How do I explain that I'm me?

593
00:40:03,442 --> 00:40:06,404
You said when your parents died,

594
00:40:06,487 --> 00:40:09,073
you handled the funeral alone
because you had no relatives.

595
00:40:09,156 --> 00:40:12,410
But it looks like you have an uncle.

596
00:40:14,787 --> 00:40:15,621
Huh?

597
00:40:18,040 --> 00:40:19,625
Now you don't even remember that?

598
00:40:20,209 --> 00:40:21,335
What uncle?

599
00:40:23,087 --> 00:40:24,171
I don't have an uncle.

600
00:40:28,759 --> 00:40:31,387
When we track down bastards
who skip out on loans,

601
00:40:31,470 --> 00:40:34,390
we dig up everything,
even all their relatives and their exes.

602
00:40:34,473 --> 00:40:36,892
That's what makes us
more competent than the police.

603
00:40:39,937 --> 00:40:41,647
Get up, you fucking bastard.

604
00:40:48,904 --> 00:40:51,073
I'll have you meet
the uncle you never had.

605
00:40:51,157 --> 00:40:55,035
If you're not Je Moon-jae there either,

606
00:40:56,495 --> 00:40:59,206
you're really fucking dead.

607
00:41:15,639 --> 00:41:17,600
If I'm not Je Moon-jae, then what am I?

608
00:41:18,893 --> 00:41:21,145
Why the hell are you asking me,
you bastard?

609
00:41:21,937 --> 00:41:25,357
A kidnapper, a murderer…

610
00:41:26,108 --> 00:41:28,736
You really think
that I'm this nameless rat?

611
00:41:31,447 --> 00:41:33,449
What if this uncle guy can't prove it?

612
00:41:33,532 --> 00:41:34,867
I told you.

613
00:41:35,367 --> 00:41:36,368
You'll fucking die.

614
00:41:38,078 --> 00:41:40,456
No, that's not what I meant.

615
00:41:42,666 --> 00:41:46,337
Even if I die,
I should at least have a name.

616
00:41:47,004 --> 00:41:48,881
Who am I gonna die as?

617
00:41:49,465 --> 00:41:50,424
When you die?

618
00:41:51,175 --> 00:41:52,468
You don't need a name.

619
00:41:52,551 --> 00:41:55,554
You only need a name when you're alive.

620
00:41:59,683 --> 00:42:02,978
If I had an uncle, the rat bastard
probably took care of that too.

621
00:42:04,355 --> 00:42:06,982
That's how things have been so far.
Don't you get it yet?

622
00:42:07,066 --> 00:42:09,818
Shut up and just come, punk.
I just wanna know!

623
00:42:11,070 --> 00:42:13,072
What kind of bastard you really are.

624
00:42:46,939 --> 00:42:51,402
Should've told the guy not to kill him.
We should bury him alive.

625
00:42:51,485 --> 00:42:53,487
And give him some <i>noja </i>money.

626
00:42:55,948 --> 00:42:58,117
<i>I still can't forget Dong-seok's eyes</i>

627
00:42:58,909 --> 00:43:00,911
<i>when he was buried.</i>

628
00:43:03,539 --> 00:43:05,749
But why was he buried?

629
00:43:07,167 --> 00:43:08,460
Jealousy, what else?

630
00:43:09,461 --> 00:43:12,840
Noja was the capable one,
but Dong-seok was the one who made it big.

631
00:43:12,923 --> 00:43:17,094
That must've rubbed him the wrong way.
He was acting superior to him.

632
00:43:17,177 --> 00:43:20,806
Jealousy. It's a scary thing.

633
00:43:20,889 --> 00:43:21,932
Hey.

634
00:43:22,433 --> 00:43:25,060
Tell him not to kill Noja.
I'll give him a bonus for it.

635
00:43:25,561 --> 00:43:26,854
Yes, got it.

636
00:43:27,521 --> 00:43:29,398
I have to bury him alive.

637
00:43:29,898 --> 00:43:31,108
Just like Dong-seok.

638
00:44:02,514 --> 00:44:03,599
Bastard!

639
00:44:29,833 --> 00:44:31,710
Hey. Are you okay?

640
00:45:05,202 --> 00:45:06,829
Goddamn it.

641
00:45:07,413 --> 00:45:08,455
Hey, punk.

642
00:45:12,459 --> 00:45:13,293
Get on my back.

643
00:45:13,377 --> 00:45:14,712
For fuck's sake.

644
00:45:15,671 --> 00:45:16,964
Fucking hell.

645
00:45:19,591 --> 00:45:20,759
Fuck.

646
00:45:32,479 --> 00:45:34,231
You fucking bastard!

647
00:45:50,164 --> 00:45:52,791
What is going on this late at night?

648
00:45:53,625 --> 00:45:57,045
I'm calling to report gunshots
at Manbulam.

649
00:46:15,022 --> 00:46:16,356
Fuck.

650
00:46:18,609 --> 00:46:21,028
Fucking idiot. You didn't even know
you were shot! Damn it.

651
00:46:22,946 --> 00:46:24,865
Stay awake
until we get to the hospital, punk!

652
00:46:25,491 --> 00:46:28,327
Noja. We can't go to the hospital now.

653
00:46:29,411 --> 00:46:32,623
If we get caught,
we'll take the fall for everything.

654
00:46:32,706 --> 00:46:34,917
That's better than dying, you dumbass!

655
00:46:35,501 --> 00:46:36,877
If I get caught now,

656
00:46:38,462 --> 00:46:40,672
am I supposed to live as the Rat forever?

657
00:46:44,802 --> 00:46:46,094
Hey.

658
00:46:46,178 --> 00:46:47,763
Fuck.

659
00:46:54,561 --> 00:46:55,854
Hey.

660
00:47:02,611 --> 00:47:04,404
I'll send someone. Stay out of sight!

661
00:47:10,953 --> 00:47:11,829
Fuck this!

662
00:47:21,588 --> 00:47:22,506
Hey, it's me.

663
00:47:22,589 --> 00:47:26,009
I left a guy who'd been shot
on the mountain road to Manbulam.

664
00:47:26,093 --> 00:47:27,261
Take him and save him.

665
00:47:27,845 --> 00:47:29,263
Hey, hurry up!

666
00:47:29,346 --> 00:47:31,890
You have to save him no matter what.
Got it?

667
00:48:07,134 --> 00:48:08,760
Suspect vehicle confirmed.

668
00:48:15,517 --> 00:48:16,602
<i>Follow him!</i>

669
00:48:18,395 --> 00:48:21,940
<i>Requesting confirmation</i>
<i>on a silver SUV near Manbulam. Over.</i>

670
00:48:23,567 --> 00:48:24,401
Hey, block him!

671
00:48:34,870 --> 00:48:36,038
<i>Suspect vehicle fleeing.</i>

672
00:48:36,121 --> 00:48:38,206
<i>Requesting patrol car at scene. Over.</i>

673
00:48:41,251 --> 00:48:42,127
Chase him. Hurry!

674
00:48:50,719 --> 00:48:52,137
Entering Hwajeong Intersection.

675
00:48:54,765 --> 00:48:58,143
Suspect vehicle direction confirmed.
Will block escape route.

676
00:49:13,992 --> 00:49:18,914
<i>Suspect vehicle fleeing toward town.</i>
<i>All units assist. Over.</i>

677
00:49:48,360 --> 00:49:49,277
Shit!

678
00:50:00,914 --> 00:50:02,791
<i>Suspect vehicle is in the alley!</i>

679
00:50:13,510 --> 00:50:14,553
<i>Blocking escape route.</i>

680
00:50:36,450 --> 00:50:38,243
Just ram it!

681
00:51:50,816 --> 00:51:52,526
PROVE IT. OR I'LL KILL YOU.

682
00:51:52,609 --> 00:51:54,111
"Uncle."

683
00:51:54,861 --> 00:51:56,071
"Han Hui-su."

684
00:52:05,580 --> 00:52:06,790
It's a pretty big amount.

685
00:52:07,499 --> 00:52:08,625
I know, right?

686
00:52:31,982 --> 00:52:34,317
Here…

687
00:52:35,318 --> 00:52:36,153
Here…

688
00:52:38,864 --> 00:52:39,739
Here…

689
00:58:00,059 --> 00:58:02,979
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
